# llama.cpp upstream pin.
#
# Format: four lines. `tag` is the human-readable upstream release (used
# in release notes and the NOTICE row), `commit` is the full 40-char sha
# that build scripts actually check out (tags move, shas don't), and
# `build` is the build number the compiled binary reports.
#
# Upstream runs TWO tag lines off the same history:
#   * `vX.Y.Z`  — semver *stable* releases (GitHub "latest"), introduced
#                 with v0.3.0. This is what we pin.
#   * `b####`   — rolling build tags, cut several times a day and now
#                 published as GitHub *prereleases*. Every stable release
#                 also carries a `b####` tag on the identical commit
#                 (v0.3.0 == b10621).
#
# `build` exists because llama.cpp derives its reported version from
# `git rev-list --count HEAD` (cmake/build-info.cmake), which used to be
# readable straight off a `b####` tag and no longer is. Both
# native/scripts/fetch-upstream.sh and scripts/assert-llama-version.mjs
# verify the built binary against it, so it must be stated explicitly
# rather than inferred. Keep all four lines in step on a bump.
#
# Verify the commit is reachable from the tag:
#   git ls-remote https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp.git refs/tags/<tag>^{}
#
# License: MIT (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp)
upstream=https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp.git
tag=v0.3.0
build=10621
commit=c1d0e7a004015f23bc0233470b747b596f29b264
